nd":"Baker County.","text":"Baker County."},{"key":"d7724084","lang":"en","send":"Spalding County.","text":"Spalding County."},{"key":"d8e88dbe","lang":"en","send":"Monroe County.","text":"Monroe County."},{"key":"dd12b4ec","lang":"en","send":"Troup County.","text":"Troup County."},{"key":"dec3823c","lang":"en","send":"Walker County.","text":"Walker County."},{"key":"df0c466a","lang":"en","send":"Pierce County.","text":"Pierce County."},{"key":"e1b5a8e9","lang":"en","send":"Irwin County.","text":"Irwin County."},{"key":"e23ab9df","lang":"en","send":"McDuffie County.","text":"McDuffie County."},{"key":"e2d70ea4","lang":"en","send":"Jefferson County.","text":"Jefferson County."},{"key":"e4416744","lang":"en","send":"Camden County.","text":"Camden County."},{"key":"e4481559","lang":"en","send":"Dont mix up: Georgia judges are elected (nonpartisan); US federal judges are appointed for life.","text":"Dont mix up: Georgia judges are elected (nonpartisan); US federal judges are appointed for life."},{"key":"e5c1577e","lang":"en","send":"Wheeler County.","text":"Wheeler County."},{"key":"e613c463","lang":"en","send":"Rockdale County.","text":"Rockdale County."},{"key":"e620bae4","lang":"en","send":"Greene County.","text":"Greene County."},{"key":"e7587e94","lang":"en","send":"Chatham County. home of Savannah and its port","text":"Chatham County. home of Savannah and its port"},{"key":"e802dbb8","lang":"en","send":"Henry County.","text":"Henry County."},{"key":"e8b3750d","lang":"en","send":"Union County.","text":"Union County."},{"key":"ea066117","lang":"en","send":"Peach County.","text":"Peach County."},{"key":"eaa05ce1","lang":"en","send":"Warren County.","text":"Warren County."},{"key":"ead1aad2","lang":"en","send":"Ben Hill County.","text":"Ben Hill County."},{"key":"eca4fea0","lang":"en","send":"Clayton County.","text":"Clayton County."},{"key":"edfa35c0","lang":"en","send":"Elbert County.","text":"Elbert County."},{"key":"ee2b21a4","lang":"en","send":"General Assembly. Makes the laws and passes the budget. Two chambers: the Senate (56 senators) and the House of Representatives (180 representatives). All serve 2-year terms. Qualifications: senators at least 25, representatives at least 21; US citizens; Georgia residents for 2 years and district residents for 1 year. Meets every year from the second Monday in January for 40 legislative days — usually into late March or early April. Leaders: the lieutenant governor presides over the Senate; the House elects its own Speaker. Committees (Education, Appropriations, Judiciary…) study every bill first — most bills never leave committee. Spending and tax bills must start in the House.","text":"General Assembly. Makes the laws and passes the budget. Two chambers: the Senate (56 senators) and the House of Representatives (180 representatives). All serve 2-year terms. Qualifications: senators at least 25, representatives at least 21; US citizens; Georgia residents for 2 years and district residents for 1 year. Meets every year from the second Monday in January for 40 legislative days — usually into late March or early April. Leaders: the lieutenant governor presides over the Senate; the House elects its own Speaker. Committees (Education, Appropriations, Judiciary…) study every bill first — most bills never leave committee. Spending and tax bills must start in the House."},{"key":"efc2142c","lang":"en","send":"Paulding County.","text":"Paulding County."},{"key":"f01a85c6","lang":"en","send":"Cherokee County.","text":"Cherokee County."},{"key":"f20176ea","lang":"en","send":"Thomas County.","text":"Thomas County."},{"key":"f21e6901","lang":"en","send":"Jones County.","text":"Jones County."},{"key":"f52d078e","lang":"en","send":"Brooks County.","text":"Brooks County."},{"key":"f820d57d","lang":"en","send":"Berrien County.","text":"Berrien County."},{"key":"fa84ee91","lang":"en","send":"Bleckley County.","text":"Bleckley County."},{"key":"fb604a30","lang":"en","send":"Washington County.","text":"Washington County."},{"key":"ff269a04","lang":"en","send":"Jeff Davis County.","text":"Jeff Davis County."},{"key":"ff4db1cd","lang":"en","send":"Early County.","text":"Early County."},{"key":"ff7fcbb9","lang":"en","send":"The Courts. Interprets the laws and administers justice. Supreme Court: 9 justices — the highest court; it decides questions about the constitution and reviews the most serious cases. Court of Appeals: 15 judges who check trial courts for legal mistakes. Trial courts: superior (felonies, divorce, land), state, juvenile, probate (wills, marriage licenses) and magistrate (warrants, small claims). Judges are chosen in nonpartisan elections — no party label on the ballot. When a seat opens early, the governor appoints a judge. Dual purpose: interpret what the laws mean, and administer justice by deciding cases fairly.","text":"The Courts. Interprets the laws and administers justice. Supreme Court: 9 justices — the highest court; it decides questions about the constitution and reviews the most serious cases. Court of Appeals: 15 judges who check trial courts for legal mistakes. Trial courts: superior (felonies, divorce, land), state, juvenile, probate (wills, marriage licenses) and magistrate (warrants, small claims). Judges are chosen in nonpartisan elections — no party label on the ballot. When a seat opens early, the governor appoints a judge. Dual purpose: interpret what the laws mean, and administer justice by deciding cases fairly."},{"key":"01a3c06e","lang":"zh","send":"Monroe 县。","text":"Monroe 县."},{"key":"02f1cb10","lang":"zh","send":"格林县。海岸城市不伦瑞克所在地","text":"格林县. 海岸城市不伦瑞克所在地"},{"key":"05d38f0a","lang":"zh","send":"Morgan 县。","text":"Morgan 县."},{"key":"07660f21","lang":"zh","send":"Hart 县。","text":"Hart 县."},{"key":"09a353ac","lang":"zh","send":"Wilcox 县。","text":"Wilcox 县."},{"key":"0a9a26f3","lang":"zh","send":"克拉克县。雅典所在地——面积最小的县","text":"克拉克县. 雅典所在地——面积最小的县"},{"key":"0ad7a7be","lang":"zh","send":"Gilmer 县。","text":"Gilmer 县."},{"key":"0c